| annot("FIX-COWORK-SIGNAL-FILENAME-CYCLEID-KEYING";
      "po_measurement_20260730T2148";
      "MEASURED CORROBORATION + a second, worse symptom than filename collision. (A) FREQUENCY: the identical 8-file set bctc_signal_{BID,FPT,FRT,GEX,HPG,MWG,VCB,VIX}_20260730_routine.json was drained and routed-to-po FOUR times on 2026-07-30 alone - commits c0cbb756f, 236310900 (18:07Z), 23aeea6ed (21:07Z), 072541471 (21:37Z) - i.e. 32 PO-triage routing events for 8 distinct facts, plus a 5th earlier drain (4737c562d 01:17Z) on a different ticker set. Date-only keying is the mechanism: the filename carries no time/cycle component, so every cycle rewrites the same path. (B) THE WORSE SYMPTOM, not previously on this row: the re-written files are NOT byte-identical re-emissions - they are DIFFERENT ANALYSES WITH A DIFFERENT FIELD SCHEMA overwriting each other at the same path. `git diff 236310900 23aeea6ed -- docs/signals/processed/bctc_signal_HPG_20260730_routine.json` shows the 18:07Z revision carrying esc3_guard_held/esc4_result/esc5_result/e3_cache/trick_summary/trick_confidence/kd_reading/cycle_id/generated_at and the 21:07Z revision carrying NONE of them (different prose, different keys, only esc3_status survives); the BID pair shows the same instability (quarantine/kd_durability replaced by roe_pct/pe/valuation_verdict/kinhdich{}/report_overdue/cycle_tick_utc/slot). Any downstream consumer parsing these fields breaks non-deterministically depending on which cycle last wrote the file, and the prior cycle's analysis survives only in git. Fix scope should therefore cover the emitter's field CONTRACT (a stable schema) alongside the filename keying - cycle-id keying alone preserves every revision but leaves consumers unable to parse them. next_agent=ba is still right.")
